  "body": "Part of #894.\n\nThe thread-milling kernel (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/thread_mill.rs`, `thread_ride.rs`) cuts an external thread on a boss - depth 0.6134 x pitch (ISO 965-1), clockwise climb under M3, quarter-arc leads from one tool radius outside the centre circle - and is pinned by `machining2d::thread_tests` and the golden `thread_mill_external_single_form.cl`. The `Thread` operation never asks for it: `operation::thread_op::kernel_params` passes `external: false`.\n\n**What is missing**\n- A feature list for bosses: recognition of vertical convex cylinders (the hole recogniser reads concave ones only) or a pick, giving centre, major radius, top and shoulder Z.\n- An `external` flag on the operation (params, file, page, MCP params), and the door's external half (a boss thinner than the thread is deep).\n- The crest law for a boss: the static footprint region cannot judge a tool standing beside a boss that rises from a wider base, so the tangency law needs the model's section at depth with the thread depth as its allowance; the root law (`thread_op::root_cutter`) must take the external depth.\n- The air around the boss: the ride feeds down beside it, which the stock and plunge laws must accept only where earlier operations cleared it.\n\n**Done means:** a Thread operation set to external threads a modelled boss, verifies clean against the part and the stock left by the operations before it, and posts helical G2/G3 with Z; a boss thinner than the thread depth and a boss with no cleared air around it are refused by name; pinned by an app test and a golden.\n",
